{"id": "EUVD-2026-98710", "enisaUuid": "ab11acb6-e587-367a-ba6e-3b301d783116", "description": "FreeRDP 3.0.0 before 3.32.0 contains a heap use-after-free vulnerability in smartcard emulation when SCARD_IOCTL_DISCONNECT and SCARD_IOCTL_TRANSMIT operate concurrently on one card handle. A malicious RDP server can overlap these IRPs through separate context workers to free and reuse the SCardHandle, causing client-process heap corruption and termination.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T13:54:06", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-8rpr-jjjg-5qv6", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.0.0-before-3.32.0-smartcard-use-after-free-via-concurrent-disconnect-and-transmit"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109945", "GHSA-f55c-wf6q-wcjx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "83d44ea5-ebf2-33a6-8eb8-dcd767a771f0", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5bb06e59-fecf-31af-8ebc-5f29112a6b9d", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}